Notebook[
 {Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["HEPCAT SYMBOL", "PacletNameCell"],
       Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["HEPCAT", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/HEPCAT"], "  \[Bullet]  ",
          ButtonBox["Related Guide", BaseStyle -> "Link",
           ButtonData -> "paclet:HEPCAT/guide/FormattingAndExport"]}],
        "AnchorBar"]}}, GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.42], Scaled[0.58]}}]],
   "AnchorBarGrid"], Cell["WriteSPINASProcess", "ObjectName"],
  Cell["Writes a complete, readable C++ process using SPINAS, with optional \
CalcHEP and MadGraph validation and numerical integration.", "Notes"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"WriteSPINASProcess", "[", "directory",
         ",", " ", "particles", ",", " ", "amplitude", ",", " ", "model",
         "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "exports one all-incoming amplitude \
at its fixed massless helicities."}], "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"WriteSPINASProcess", "[", "directory",
         ",", " ", "entries", ",", " ", "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"],
     "  ", "combines helicity-related {particles, amplitude} entries into one \
class."}], "Usage"],
  Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"WriteSPINASProcess", "[", "directory",
         ",", " ", "incoming", " ", "->", " ", "outgoing", ",", " ",
         "entries", ",", " ", "model", "]"}]], "InlineFormula"], "  ", "decla\
res the physical process and crosses its outgoing legs automatically."}],
   "Usage"], Cell["Details", "NotesSection"], Cell["Inputs are symbolic \
all-incoming amplitudes. In the physical-process form, the concatenated \
incoming and outgoing lists fix the external-leg order, while each amplitude \
entry retains its all-incoming particle list. Do not pre-cross these \
formulas.", "Notes"], Cell["For example, a physical e,A -> e,A process has \
all-incoming species e,A,E,A. Outgoing momenta and angle-spinor signs are \
crossed exactly once by the exporter.", "Notes"],
  Cell["A generic massless name such as A requests its complete helicity sum. \
A.+, A.- or the string option \"FixedHelicities\" selects a specified \
helicity. Incomplete requested coverage is refused; missing amplitudes are \
not invented using parity.", "Notes"], Cell["Generated amp returns the \
complex amplitude for one external spin/helicity assignment. spin_sum adds \
|amp| squared over the requested states. Family amp2 also averages unfixed \
incoming states and applies the final identical-species factor once, \
including identical fermions.", "Notes"], Cell["The older fixed-helicity \
overload preserves its existing normalization convention. Use the \
physical-process or family form for a complete unpolarized process.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Generated examples and random validation points use stable \
physical two-body kinematics, including known-mass light-cone components for \
boosted decay products. This numerical mass-shell information belongs to the \
generated external particles and decay construction; it does not place \
virtual propagators on shell. Known external momentum squares use their \
declared masses, and supported external scalar products use the stable \
particle contraction with crossing signs retained. General composite squares \
and scalar products remain off shell.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The default export writes source only. \"Build\" -> True compiles and \
links the existing SPINAS library; \"RunExamples\" -> True also runs three \
conserved physical example points. No external library is installed or \
rebuilt.", "Notes"], Cell["\"SPINASDirectory\" and \"CMakeExecutable\" \
support automatic build-tool discovery. Independent validation instead \
requires an explicit reference-generator directory and model selection. The \
SPINAS precision must match the library ABI. \"Overwrite\" -> True explicitly \
permits replacing an existing exported project.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The independent CalcHEP validator generates a reference process and \
compares common random points. Specify \"CalcHEPDirectory\" and \
\"CalcHEPModel\" -> {directory, modelNumber}; both default to None. \
\"CalcHEPAllowedParticles\" -> All retains the full chosen theory, while an \
explicit list of positive absolute PDGs restricts the reference particle \
sector. \"RunCalcHEPValidation\" -> True builds and runs it. The actual \
time-based seed is reported, and an explicit \"CalcHEPSeed\" or --seed value \
replays it.", "Notes"], Cell["A separate n_calchep target uses the SPINAS \
matrix element with CalcHEP's numerical phase-space integration, cuts, \
histograms and VEGAS. This bypasses symbolic CalcHEP generation and does not \
require an equivalent CalcHEPModel. The build copies its actual executable to \
results/n_calchep in the exported project. Enter results and run ./n_calchep \
for the numerical session. Validation and example executables stay in build. \
The results executable is not a symlink back to build; installed CalcHEP and \
system runtime dependencies remain required.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Numerical model constraints, masses and widths are connected to the \
numerical menus. Explicit amplitude width conventions remain authoritative. \
Unsupported automatic-width or gauge-restoring operations are refused.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Current complete numerical exports are colorless. \
Unresolved Xi spinors, hats, unsupported symbolic functions or color tensors \
must be resolved before exporting.", "Notes"], Cell["The independent MadGraph \
validator generates one unpolarized reference process and compares each \
exported massless-helicity combination separately. \"RunMadGraphValidation\" \
-> True builds and runs the check; \"MadGraphPoints\" -> 1000 and \
\"MadGraphSeed\" -> Automatic are the normal defaults. Massive external spins \
are summed because the two libraries may use different spin bases.",
   "Notes"], Cell["Specify \"MadGraphDirectory\" and \"MadGraphModel\" \
explicitly to select the independent reference generator and UFO theory; both \
default to None. \"MadGraphAllowedParticles\" -> All retains the full chosen \
model, or a list such as {11, 22} explicitly selects the \
electron/positron/photon sector. \"MadGraphParameterRules\" supplies external \
UFO input values when numerical matching needs an override. No theory or \
particle restriction is inferred from the HEPCAT process.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Generated projects contain validate_madgraph(options) and a \
process_validate_madgraph executable. ValidateMadGraph provides the \
corresponding Mathematica entry point, including a simple per-helicity table \
and optional detailed numerical diagnostics. MadGraph is not required for \
ordinary SPINAS evaluation.", "Notes"], Cell["The same export also supplies a \
MadEvent numerical bridge. Independent MadGraph validation evaluates \
MadGraph's own matrix element; the MadEvent bridge instead evaluates the \
supplied HEPCAT/SPINAS amplitude inside MadEvent's leading-order integration \
and event-generation workflow. Both use the explicitly selected MadGraph \
installation, UFO model and particle restriction.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The selected UFO model supplies MadEvent's particle information, \
numerical parameter definitions and phase-space topologies. The HEPCAT/SPINAS \
expression remains the numerical matrix element. Running the numerical bridge \
does not by itself establish agreement with MadGraph's independent \
expression; use the separate validation report for that comparison.",
   "Notes"], Cell["MadEvent retains its phase-space weights, flux, beam and \
cut handling, integration and event generation. The bridge must apply the \
incoming-state average and final identical-particle factor exactly once. \
Fixed massless helicities remain selected contributions; their normalization \
is not replaced by an unpolarized result.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The initial MadEvent bridge supports colorless leading-order tree \
processes supported by the SPINAS exporter. It does not generate virtual \
corrections, subtraction terms or a matched next-to-leading-order \
calculation. Massive SPINAS spin labels must not be interpreted as MadGraph \
helicity-basis or production-decay correlation data. Massive event spins are \
left unspecified; a massive polarized beam is not supported by this bridge.",
   "Notes"], Cell["\"MadGraphParameterMap\" maps HEPCAT parameter names to \
differently named UFO parameters. Used couplings and masses are checked \
rather than assumed from the external particle names.", "Notes"],
  Cell["MadGraph propagator widths are matched to the amplitude prescription. \
For bare HEPCAT PropDen denominators, unmatched adjustable reference widths \
are zeroed; explicit reference width rules and matched width parameters are \
preserved. Detailed validation reports record this choice.", "Notes"],
  Cell["The return value is the output directory. \"ReturnDetails\" -> True \
adds generated file paths, build information, normalization metadata and \
optional validation results.", "Notes"], Cell["When both independent \
reference checks are requested, both are attempted even if one fails. A \
requested numerical FAIL, unavailable reference or runtime error returns \
Failure; its ExportResult contains the generated project and both reference \
reports. Writing source or finishing compilation is not reported as a \
physics-validation success.", "Notes"], Cell["With MadGraph configured, the \
exporter writes madevent-spinas.cpp, madevent-runtime.py, \
madevent-config.json and a small launcher. \"Build\" -> True builds the \
process_madevent_matrix static library and build/process_madevent executable, \
with process replaced by ProcessName. MadEvent topology generation is \
deferred until the launcher is used.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Enter the exported project's build directory and run \
./process_madevent --prepare to create a MadEvent session inside that working \
directory. Use ./process_madevent for its interactive interface, \
--command-file path for a standard MadEvent command file, or --run run_name \
to generate events with the current cards. The default session is \
PROC_<ProcessName>, such as PROC_eeAA, under the directory from which the \
launcher is run; --work-directory DIR selects another workspace. The launcher \
prints full card, HTML and event-output locations. Existing sessions \
elsewhere remain untouched.", "Notes"], Cell["Within the chosen workspace, \
PROC_eeAA/Cards/run_card.dat and param_card.dat control the numerical eeAA \
run, PROC_eeAA/index.html opens the HTML pages, and PROC_eeAA/Events/run_name \
contains its generated events. The directory name follows ProcessName for \
other processes. Repeated launches from the same workspace retain its cards \
and results. Current evaluated UFO parameters are passed to SPINAS at every \
matrix-element call, so supported coupling and mass changes take effect \
without rebuilding the exported amplitude. Changing a spinning external \
particle between massive and massless requires a new export.", "Notes"],
  Cell["Once --prepare finishes, the complete PROC_<ProcessName> directory \
can be moved or copied. Start bin/madevent inside that directory. Its \
required HEPCAT/SPINAS amplitude sources, headers, numerical libraries and \
private model support are included, so the original exported project, build \
directory and SPINAS checkout are no longer required by the prepared \
numerical process. The outer process_madevent executable remains the initial \
preparation launcher. MadGraph, Python, a compatible Fortran toolchain and \
system libraries remain external prerequisites. Move a session between runs \
while it is idle.", "Notes"], Cell["Options", "NotesSection"],
  Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{{Cell["Option", "TableHeader"],
       Cell["Default", "TableHeader"], Cell["Meaning", "TableHeader"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"SPINASDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Path to the local SPINAS \
checkout/library. Automatic searches SPINAS_ROOT and the sibling spinas \
checkout; an explicit directory selects another installation.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"IncomingLegs\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", "1", ",", " ", "2", "}"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["External leg labels that \
are physically incoming in exported C++. Other legs are crossed once from \
HEPCAT's all-ingoing convention, including outgoing angle-spinor signs. \
Runnable projects currently require two incoming particles.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"FixedHelicities\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Massless \
leg-to-doubled-helicity rules selecting states in the grouped SPINAS \
exporter. Automatic retains the requested coverage; explicitly fixed incoming \
helicities are not averaged over, and a fixed outgoing helicity is a labeled \
contribution.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Local numerical parameter \
overrides keyed by model references or string names. Automatic resolves the \
model's variables and dependent functions; fitting and checks do not assign \
global values or replace parameters in the symbolic final amplitude.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ProcessName\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"hepcat_process\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Valid C++ identifier for \
the exported SPINAS class and executable. Choose a readable process name that \
does not collide with reserved generated members.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Precision\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Floating-point type used \
by exported SPINAS code. Automatic reads the local library build \
configuration; \"Double\" and \"LongDouble\" must match the library being \
linked.", "TableText"]}, {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Build\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to configure and compile the exported C++ \
project against the existing SPINAS library. False writes source files only; \
a source-only export does not require CMake.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunExamples\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to build the exported SPINAS project and \
execute its sample phase-space points. True implies the necessary build \
step.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CMakeExecutable\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Path to the CMake program \
used when building. Automatic searches PATH and standard installations, \
including common macOS application and Homebrew locations.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"Overwrite\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether existing generated project files may be \
replaced. False protects an existing SPINAS output directory from accidental \
overwriting.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen CalcHEP installation directory. None, the \
default, leaves the optional backend unconfigured. An explicitly supplied \
Automatic consults the corresponding environment variables only; no \
installation path is guessed.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPModel\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen equivalent CalcHEP reference theory as \
{directory, modelNumber}. None, the default, selects no theory; Automatic \
does not infer a model. This reference model is separate from the supplied \
HEPCAT amplitudes.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPAllowedParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"All"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["All retains the full selected CalcHEP theory. A \
nonempty list of unique positive absolute PDG codes restricts the independent \
reference particle sector, including antiparticles. Every external type must \
be included.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunCalcHEPValidation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether export builds and runs the generated \
independent CalcHEP comparison. It uses the same physical points on both \
implementations; unsupported polarized or color-stripped comparisons report \
unavailable. When MadGraph is also requested, its check still runs if CalcHEP \
fails. A failed requested reference returns Failure with both reports \
retained in ExportResult.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPPoints\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"1000"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Number of random physical phase-space points \
compared by the generated independent CalcHEP validation executable. This \
tests both implementations at the same points.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"CalcHEPSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Default seed of the \
generated CalcHEP comparison. Automatic chooses from the time when validation \
runs and prints the concrete seed; an unsigned 64-bit integer, including \
zero, makes the run reproducible.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"ReturnDetails\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether to expose optional diagnostic data \
instead of the compact default result. For preparation and factorization \
completion it retains provenance, directions and validation and takes \
precedence over Output; for export it returns file paths and build/run \
results.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphDirectory\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen MadGraph installation directory for \
independent validation and the MadEvent numerical bridge. None, the default, \
leaves this optional support unconfigured. An explicitly supplied Automatic \
consults environment variables only; pass a path to make the selection \
explicit.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphModel\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"None"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Chosen MadGraph UFO model name or directory. It \
supplies the independent validation reference and the numerical MadEvent \
model metadata and phase-space topologies. None, the default, selects no \
theory; Automatic does not infer one. Specify the model and any particle \
filter explicitly.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphAllowedParticles\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"All"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["All retains the full selected MadGraph theory. A \
nonempty list of unique positive absolute PDG codes, such as {11,22}, \
restricts the particle sector used for reference validation and MadEvent \
topology generation and includes antiparticles. Every external particle type \
must be present.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphParameterRules\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Real numerical values for \
named external MadGraph UFO parameters. Automatic uses the supported \
model-parameter matching; explicit rules supply otherwise ambiguous \
independent inputs.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphParameterMap\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Rules mapping HEPCAT model \
parameter names to external or derived MadGraph UFO parameter names. \
Automatic uses supported same-name and known-model matching; unresolved used \
parameters prevent a passing comparison.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"RunMadGraphValidation\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"False"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Whether WriteSPINASProcess builds and runs the \
independent MadGraph comparison. False writes the optional support without \
running it; True runs a report for each exported massless-helicity \
combination. A numerical FAIL is returned as Failure, not a successful \
source-export result. If CalcHEP is also requested, both checks are attempted \
and their reports remain in ExportResult.", "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphPoints\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"1000"}]], "InlineFormula"]}],
        "TableText"], Cell["Number of common random phase-space points \
compared for each massless-helicity combination. The default is 1000.",
        "TableText"]},
      {Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"\"MadGraphSeed\""}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"],
       Cell[TextData[{Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Automatic"}]],
           "InlineFormula"]}], "TableText"], Cell["Random seed for the \
generated MadGraph comparison. Automatic chooses one time-based seed when \
validation runs and reports it; an explicit unsigned 64-bit integer, \
including zero, replays the samples.", "TableText"]}},
     GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {Left, Left, Left}},
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {Scaled[0.23], Scaled[0.19],
         Scaled[0.58]}}, GridBoxDividers ->
      {"Rows" -> {False, True, {False}, False}}]], "3ColumnTableMod"],
  Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"],
  Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Load HEPCAT", "ExampleSubsection"],
     Cell["Evaluate this setup once before the examples. The paths refer to \
the local HEPCAT checkout; no model parameters are assigned global numerical \
values.", "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"If", "[", "!", "StringQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", " ", "||", " ", "!", "DirectoryQ",
         "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ",
         "Global`$HEPCATpath", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "First", "[", "PacletFind", "[", "\"HEPCAT\"", "]", "]", "[",
         "\"Location\"", "]", ",", " ", "\"source\"", "}", "]", "]", ";",
         "\n", "If", "[", "!", "MemberQ", "[", "$Packages", ",", " ",
         "\"ConstructiveDiagrams`\"", "]", ",", "\n", " ", " ", "Get", "[",
         "FileNameJoin", "[", "{", "Global`$HEPCATpath", ",", " ",
         "\"HEPCAT.wl\"", "}", "]", "]", "]", ";", "\n", "hepcatDirectory",
         " ", "=", " ", "ParentDirectory", "[", "Global`$HEPCATpath", "]",
         ";", "\n", "modelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[",
         "{", "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"models\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n",
         "feynmanModelDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin", "[", "{",
         "hepcatDirectory", ",", " ", "\"model_feynman\"", "}", "]", ";"}]],
      "Input", InitializationCell -> True]}, Open]],
  Cell["Basic Examples", "ExampleSection"],
  Cell["Inspect the available export options without writing files.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Options", "[", "WriteSPINASProcess",
      "]"}]], "Input"], Cell["Export a complete four-point photon-helicity \
family to a temporary directory.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"knownModel", " ", "=", " ", "ReadModel", "[",
      "modelDirectory", ",", " ", "3", "]", ";", "\n", "helicityProcesses",
      " ", "=", " ", "{", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ",
      "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", "}", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ",
      "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"", "}", ",", " ", "{",
      "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"", ",", " ", "\"A.+\"",
      "}", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", ",", " ", "\"A.-\"",
      ",", " ", "\"A.-\"", "}", "}", ";", "\n", "entries", " ", "=", " ",
      "{", "#", ",", " ", "LookupAmplitude", "[", "Thread", "[", "{", "#",
      ",", " ", "Range", "[", "4", "]", "}", "]", ",", " ", "knownModel",
      ",", " ", "False", ",", " ", "{", "i", ",", " ", "j", ",", " ", "k",
      ",", " ", "l", "}", "]", "}", " ", "&", " ", "/@", " ",
      "helicityProcesses", ";", "\n", "exportDirectory", " ", "=", " ",
      "CreateDirectory", "[", "]", ";", "\n", "WriteSPINASProcess", "[",
      "exportDirectory", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", "}", " ",
      "->", " ", "{", "\"A\"", ",", " ", "\"A\"", "}", ",", " ", "entries",
      ",", " ", "knownModel", ",", " ", "\"ProcessName\"", " ", "->", " ",
      "\"eeAA\"", "]"}]], "Input"], Cell["This example writes files, starts a \
longer calculation, or requires an optional external tool. Evaluate it when \
you want to perform that operation.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell["Optionally build the exported project and run its example points.",
   "ExampleText"], Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"WriteSPINASProcess", "[",
      "exportDirectory", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", "}", " ",
      "->", " ", "{", "\"A\"", ",", " ", "\"A\"", "}", ",", " ", "entries",
      ",", " ", "knownModel", ",", " ", "\"ProcessName\"", " ", "->", " ",
      "\"eeAA\"", ",", " ", "\"Overwrite\"", " ", "->", " ", "True", ",",
      " ", "\"Build\"", " ", "->", " ", "True", ",", " ", "\"RunExamples\"",
      " ", "->", " ", "True", "]"}]], "Input"],
  Cell["This example writes files, starts a longer calculation, or requires \
an optional external tool. Evaluate it when you want to perform that \
operation.", "ExampleText"], Cell["Generate the independent per-helicity \
MadGraph report while exporting. Set the directory and model to your chosen \
installation and theory; this example explicitly selects the \
electron/positron/photon sector of sm-full.", "ExampleText"],
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"madGraphDirectory", " ", "=", " ", "FileNameJoin",
      "[", "{", "ParentDirectory", "[", "hepcatDirectory", "]", ",", " ",
      "\"MadGraph\"", "}", "]", ";", "\n", "WriteSPINASProcess", "[",
      "exportDirectory", ",", " ", "{", "\"e\"", ",", " ", "\"E\"", "}", " ",
      "->", " ", "{", "\"A\"", ",", " ", "\"A\"", "}", ",", " ", "entries",
      ",", " ", "knownModel", ",", " ", "\"ProcessName\"", " ", "->", " ",
      "\"eeAA\"", ",", " ", "\"Overwrite\"", " ", "->", " ", "True", ",",
      " ", "\"MadGraphDirectory\"", " ", "->", " ", "madGraphDirectory", ",",
      " ", "\"MadGraphModel\"", " ", "->", " ", "\"sm-full\"", ",", " ",
